<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    ROT_LIVE_PREPARATIONS_1 — the eight live preparations (M4, bans 4).
    Three teas, four symbionts, one export payload.

    BAN 4 IS ENFORCED BY THE ENGINE, NOT BY DISCIPLINE. Every def in this
    file carries BOTH:

      CompProperties_TemperatureRuinable  minSafeTemperature 8 °C — a fridge
        RUINS it. (VERIFIED this pass: RimWorld/CompTemperatureRuinable.cs
        adds ruinedPercent whenever AmbientTemperature < minSafeTemperature,
        broadcasts RuinedByTemperature at 100%, and renders the "Freezing:
        n%" inspect line for free.) maxSafeTemperature is left at vanilla's
        100 °C default: heat is not the threat the sheet describes.
      CompProperties_Lifespan             lifespanTicks 150000 — 2.5 in-game
        days (60,000 ticks/day), then it is gone. Delay kills.

    Both are VANILLA comps on purpose. The obvious build was an RM_ subclass
    carrying the strict/lenient threshold, but mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards
    is not in the live mod list (ENVHAZARDS_NEVER_ACTIVATED_1), a
    MayRequire'd <li> would simply drop, and the teas would quietly become
    storable — ban 4 defeated by a mod-list decision nobody connected to it.
    With vanilla comps the ban holds on any install at all, and the lenient
    OPTION is a patch in that mod on top (RM_Patch_LivePrepViability).

    tickerType Rare on every def: both comps tick through CompTickRare, and
    without it neither clock runs at all.

    MODEXTENSIONS, both MayRequire'd on the <li> (never on a def or an
    Operation — kit law):
      RM_LivePrepExtension      the live-prep tag. Read by the lenient
                                option, and by selftest_live_prep.py, which
                                FAILS if a def carrying it lacks either comp
                                above — the linter this ticket demands.
      RM_TreasureMarkerExtension  owner card 6: selling this is "selling a
                                part of yourself". The tag is matched by
                                RUT_RotTreasureConscience (Defs/Misc/).

    SCARCITY (card 1: "darned hard to obtain even with pilgrimage"):
    stackLimit 5, one brew per bill, six ingredient units per brew against a
    plant harvestYield of 3. MarketValue is high and tradeability Sellable
    precisely so card 6's conscience has something to bite on — a treasure
    nobody would sell is not a temptation.

    ART OWED: every texPath here is a PLACEHOLDER reusing already-shipped
    RotSporeKit item art. Bespoke sprites owed for all eight.
    ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  -->

  <!-- ══════════════════ TEA 1 — AGE REVERSAL (owner card 1) ══════════════════
       5 biological years on the first cup, capped at adult, and a pawn can
       benefit only once per year. All three clauses live in the doer's
       fields below; satedDurationTicks 3600000 = 60,000 ticks/day x 60 days
       = one in-game year. The doer is MayRequire'd, so without
       environmentalhazards this is an inert (but still perishable) cup
       rather than a load error.
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <ThingDef ParentName="DrugBase">
    <defName>RUT_Tea_AgeReversal</defName>
    <label>ageless brew</label>
    <description>A thin, faintly warm liquor pressed from ageless cap flesh within minutes of cutting it. Drunk fresh, it unpicks years of accumulated damage in a single afternoon — and then the body is saturated, and will take nothing more from it for a year. Nobody has ever managed to carry a cup home.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>RotSporeKit/Things/Item/GlowGoo/GlowGoo_A</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_StackCount</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <tickerType>Rare</tickerType>
    <stackLimit>5</stackLimit>
    <tradeability>Sellable</tradeability>
    <techLevel>Neolithic</techLevel>
    <socialPropernessMatters>true</socialPropernessMatters>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>820</MarketValue>
      <Mass>0.3</Mass>
      <DeteriorationRate>8</DeteriorationRate>
      <Nutrition>0</Nutrition>
    </statBases>
    <ingestible>
      <foodType>Liquor</foodType>
      <baseIngestTicks>300</baseIngestTicks>
      <ingestCommandString>Drink {0}</ingestCommandString>
      <ingestReportString>Drinking {0}.</ingestReportString>
      <humanlikeOnly>true</humanlikeOnly>
      <outcomeDoers>
        <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_IngestionOutcomeDoer_AgeReversal" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
          <yearsReversed>5</yearsReversed>
          <satedHediff>RUT_AgeReversalSated</satedHediff>
          <satedDurationTicks>3600000</satedDurationTicks>
          <humanlikeOnly>true</humanlikeOnly>
        </li>
      </outcomeDoers>
    </ingestible>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_TemperatureRuinable">
        <minSafeTemperature>8</minSafeTemperature>
      </li>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Lifespan">
        <lifespanTicks>150000</lifespanTicks>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_LivePrepExtension" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
        <preparationFamily>RotLivePrep</preparationFamily>
      </li>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_TreasureMarkerExtension" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
        <treasureTag>RotTreasure</treasureTag>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </ThingDef>

